# Commit messages

Use short imperative sentences. Do not use Conventional Commits prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`).

- Sentence case: `Add usenet KubeVirt VM to replace ifrit`
- Lead with the outcome, not the file list
- Skip a body when the subject is enough
- Add a body only to explain *why*, not to restates the diff

```
# ❌ BAD
feat: add homepage widgets
Updated kubernetes/apps/homepage/release.yaml to enable plex.

# ✅ GOOD
Enable the Plex widget on the homepage dashboard
```

```
# ❌ BAD
chore(deps): bump talos

# ✅ GOOD
Pin Helios to Talos v1.13.9 and migrate node network off machine.network.
```

Dependency bumps follow `Update dependency <name> to v<version>`.
Action/image bumps follow `Update <name> to v<version>`.
